# 112blackmagic_target_flash_merged.patch
#
# WHY THIS PATCH EXISTS
# ---------------------
# Consolidates Target common, flash subsystem, breakpoint framework, and XML cleanup patches
# (formerly patches 11, 47, 50, 51, 53, 55, and common parts of 82bis, 85bis, 105):
#
# 1. Target Architecture & Option Tracking (formerly patch 82bis, 47):
#    Blackmagic needed a clean, unified way to tag target architectures (ARM vs RISC-V) in
#    target->target_options using bitfields (TOP_ARCH_SHIFT) so higher-level debug code can
#    determine the architecture without fragile string comparisons on target->driver.
#
# 2. Software Breakpoint Framework & Query Helpers (formerly patches 50, 51):
#    Provides generic target hooks for software breakpoints (sw_breakpoint_add, sw_breakpoint_remove)
#    and exports target_breakpoint_available() to report remaining hardware breakpoint and
#    watchpoint registers to the caller.
#
# 3. Flash Programming Error Handling & Erase Optimization (formerly patches 53, 55):
#    - Buffered flash writes must immediately abort on the first write error rather than continuing
#      to flash garbage into subsequent flash blocks.
#    - Variable size erase block support allows CH32V targets with differing sector/block sizes
#      to use the largest possible erase blocks, speeding up erase times considerably.
#
# 4. Binary Footprint & XML Generation Cleanups (formerly patches 11, 85bis, 105):
#    - Redirects printf to embedded printf to avoid bringing in full standard C library printf bloat.
#    - Adds DMI operation counters and benchmark timing fields to target struct for performance profiling.
#    - Disables obsolete C XML memory map chunk generators (mem_map_ram, mem_map_flash) in target.c
#      and target_flash.c, as zero-heap XML streaming is now done on the Rust side.
#
# FIX
# ---
# 1. In src/include/target.h:
#    - Define TOPT_GET_ARCH, TOPT_SET_ARCH, TOPT_ARCH_ARM, and TOPT_ARCH_RISCV macros.
#    - Declare sw_breakpoint hook functions and target_breakpoint_available().
#
# 2. In src/target/target.c:
#    - Implement target_breakpoint_available() and software breakpoint framework handlers.
#    - Integrate architecture options and DMI benchmark counters.
#    - Disable obsolete C mem_map XML generation functions (#if 0).
#
# 3. In src/target/target_flash.c:
#    - In target_flash_write_buffered(), immediately abort and fail if target_check_error() or
#      a block write fails.
#    - Support variable block erase sizes to accelerate flash erasing.
#    - Disable legacy C memory map XML chunk formatting.
#
# 4. In src/target/target_internal.h & target_probe.h:
#    - Declare helper prototypes for software breakpoints and option tweaking.
#
diff --git a/src/include/target.h b/src/include/target.h
